Chapter: Fat16Write

  cites Foreword chapter Fat16

 A Codex program can write a file. This is the test that says so, and it says
 it by writing one and then reading it back through a path that shares no code
 with the writer: fat16-read-text walks the directory, follows the cluster
 chain and decodes the bytes, exactly as it did before any of this existed.

 The bytes matter as much as the round trip. Codex Text is CCE internally, and
 a FAT16 short name and a file's contents are ASCII. A writer that put CCE on
 the disk would round-trip perfectly here -- our reader would decode what our
 writer encoded, and the two would agree forever -- while producing a file no
 other reader on earth could open. That is not a hypothetical: it is what
 shipped a TLS hostname and every key-schedule label in CCE. So the harness
 checks the raw bytes host-side as well, and this test pins the half it can:
 the size the directory entry records, which is a byte count and not a
 character count, and would be wrong the moment the encoding was.

 We say:

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  opening = act
    ok <- fat16-write-file "HELLO.TXT" "Hello, disk!"
    print-line-uni ("wrote " & show ok)

    there <- file-exists "HELLO.TXT"
    print-line-uni ("exists " & show there)

    vol <- fat16-init 2048
    back <- fat16-read-text vol "HELLO.TXT"
    print-line-uni ("readback " & maybe-text back)

    entry <- fat16-resolve-path vol "HELLO.TXT"
    print-line-uni ("size " & show (entry-size entry))

    bok <- fat16-write-binary-file "BIN.DAT" [1, 2, 3, 254]
    print-line-uni ("wrote-bin " & show bok)
    bytes <- fat16-read-bytes vol "BIN.DAT"
    print-line-uni ("bin " & maybe-bytes bytes)

    gone <- file-exists "NOPE.XXX"
    print-line-uni ("absent " & show gone)
  end

Section: Reporting

  maybe-text : Maybe Text -> Text
  maybe-text (m) = when m
    is Just (t) -> t
    is None -> "<none>"

  entry-size : Maybe Fat16DirEntry -> Integer
  entry-size (m) = when m
    is Just (e) -> e.de-size
    is None -> 0 - 1

  maybe-bytes : Maybe (List Integer) -> Text
  maybe-bytes (m) = when m
    is Just (bs) -> show-bytes bs 0 (list-length bs) ""
    is None -> "<none>"

  show-bytes : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  show-bytes (bs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else show-bytes bs (i + 1) n (acc & show (list-at bs i) & " ")
